Z||000000||Black88GT||10-13-2000||03:55 PM||||I have been saying I am going to do this for the past 2 years.  Being on every mailing list, forum whatever for 3 years I have really seen a need.  I feel that new fiero owners have no place to go unless a certain few people are willing to constantly answer the same questions over and over again.  It won't be anything fancy though, so don't expect to see Flash graphics or anything.  So I need everyone to help me with the questions.<P>Here is what I have so far, this is a VERY rough draft and I hope to have much much much more.  I will start with the basics...<P>--------------------------------------<P>-Is the fiero rear-engined?<P>No, it is "mid-engined".  This means the engine is in front of the rear axle.  This is ideal for weight distribution.  It is the only american mid-engined car ever mass produced.<P>-Is the Fiero fiberglass like Corvettes?<P>No, the Fiero uses 4 different types of plastic for body panels, named "Enduraflex" for marketing purposes.  <BR>SMC - Sheet Molded Compound makes up the hood, roof, rear upper quarter, and rear decklid. <BR>RRIM - Reinforced Reaction Injection Molding make up fenders, door panels, and lower rear quarters. (the rear lowers were later changed to injection molded nylon) <BR>RIM - Reaction Injection Molded Urethane is used for the facias. <BR>TPO - Thermo Plastic Olefin is used for the rocker panels. <P>-I noticed on my V-6 Fiero the TB says "Holley", is this stock?<P>No, it came from the factory...<P>-I noticed a hole where the TB bolts into the "Fiero" plenum, is that causing my erratic idle?<P>No, this was a design flaw.  The drilled a bolt in too deep causing the hole.  Most run an ignition wire over it to cover it.  This will not cause an erratic idle.<P>-Was the '88 suspension designed by lotus?<P>No, this was a rumor that was shot down by the "father of the fiero" Hulki Aldicacti himself at the Michigan Fiero Fest.<P>-Are all Fiero's fiery death traps?<P>No, the Fiero was one of the safest cars in the article "Which Cars Protect you Best?", April 1984 Consumer Reports magazine.  The Volvo DL was the only car with better ratings in this test.  The only difference between the Fiero and the the Volvo was that the Volvo had a step higher rating for structural integrity. <P>The fire part of this is not true also.  The Fiero factory was supplied with bad rods, and the original engine only held 3 qts. of oil to begin with.  When the owner let the oil get to low, the rod would fly out of the front of the block pouring oil all over the cat. convertor.  They changed this by adding a heat shield and increasing oil capacity to 4 qts.  They also replaced some engines obviously.<P>-Do 2.8L V6s have problems with spun bearings?<P>Unfortunately, yes.  The 2.8s have low end oiling problems.  <P>-A V8 is impossible to fit in the tiny Fiero!<P>Well, no not really.  Check out <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com." TARGET=_blank>www.v8archie.com.</A>   Many people have done this with success.<P>-What other engine swaps are possible.<P>Just name a GM engine!!  3.1, 3.2 (2.8 with 3.1 crank bored .030 over, or 3.1 bored .030 over) 3.4, 3.8 N/A, 3.8 SC, SBC, Quad 4, 3.4 TDC, 4.3, Cadillac Northstar.  Check out <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A>  or <A HREF="http://www.americancustomeng.com" TARGET=_blank>www.americancustomeng.com</A>  for  more info.<P>-My headlights on my '87 and/or '88 are not working properly.  Do I need to replace the motors?<P>Most likely, no.  Check out <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  for kits that replace the bushings in the headlight assembly.  This will usually cure the problem, easily and cheaply.<P>-What different tranny's were availible in the Fiero?<P>THC125 auto, 4 speed muncie 3.65 used in 86 GTs, 4 speed muncie 4.10, 5 speed Isuzu used in ALL '85 -'88 4 cyl. models, 5 speed getrag used in ALL '86.5 -'88 V6 models. <P>----------------------------------------<P>Ok thats all I have now.  I am sure I could think of more but I am getting tired of typing.  I will probably use a geocities site simply because it is free and I am familiar with the interface.<P>PLEASE contribute!!  Anything you feel is a "Frequently Asked Question" by Fiero owners and non-Fiero owners, post it!!!<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000001||Black88GT||10-13-2000||04:01 PM||||OK I have just registered<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierofaq" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fierofaq</A> <P>so it will be easy to remember.<P>Also I forgot to mention, if I made any mistakes in the ones I thought of please correct me and have hard evidence to back it up (if applicable)!  I want this to be CORRECT information!<P>thanks<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
