Z||000005||fiero56||10-16-2000||12:41 AM||||It is extremely annoying seeing the same questions posted day after day. My first suggestion, would be teach people how to use the <B>search</B> function. That, and tell everyone to get a Haynes(or other) manual, and try to figure it out on their own first. Aside from that, I think you have covered the most frequent daily threads. Another thing <B>every</B> Fiero owner should have is "The Fiero Spotters Guide"!!! It would getrid of a lot of questions about model year differences.<P>Later model 2.8s have an improved oiling system over the earlier models. It is possible to improve oiling in earlier model blocks, requires modifying bearings. Another one is externally/internally balanced 2.8s. countless tranny questions, Duke differences, 3.4/3800.||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfiero||10-16-2000||01:09 AM||||T-Tops were a factory authorized option....the cars were shipped to C&C for retrofitting (GM did not install the T-Tops themselves).  As an "official" option it got its own RPO code.....CJB.  If you have an '88 Fiero with T-Tops, look at the service sticker under the hood on the left inner fender area.<P><BR>Another telltale sign your T-Tops are "factory" is the weatherseals were actually different.  The kits that C&C sold have a separate rubber strip that attaches to the T-frame and helps hold the headliner in place.  Factory CJB T-Tops have this molded into the weatherseal.....kind of hard to explain, but if you have a molded lip on your weatherseal odds are good it's an original.<P>Also,  There is one more tranny......the '84 econo coupes got a very high geared tranny.  This helped it achieve 40+ MPG.  Only 5000 or so were ever built (I have one!), so they are uncommon.  The 4.10 ratio was more prevalent.<P>The Muncie 4-sp. used on '86 GT's was also used in '85 GT's & SE's as well as early '86 SE's.<P> <BR>Keep up the good work Jeff. <P> <BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Black88GT||10-16-2000||03:11 AM||||Yeah the t-top questions are defintely going in there.  Probably a few about production numbers and such , and giving mark corbins email address for the spotters guide. <P><BR>Geesh, it seems that my website program is MIA.  Anyone know of a good one for free that you can DL on the net???<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
